  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1253 AM MDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nModels continue to indicate a few embedded waves translating across the \nNorthern Tier through the weekend, ahead of a stronger upper low progged \nto move onshore across the PacNW on Sunday and continue across the \nIntermountain West and Northern Rockies through the middle of the week.  \n\nWith that said, another weak front passing across the plains Saturday\nmorning will bring a slight cool down to temperatures, mainly across \nthe plains. A slow increase in available moisture within the westerly\nflow aloft will bring a slight chance of high based afternoon showers \nand storms over the higher terrain, with a few shra possibly moving \nacross the I-25 Corridor late in the afternoon and early evening.  \n\nBy Sunday, available moisture continues to increase within southwesterly\nflow aloft, leading to chances of afternoon showers and storms over and \nnear the higher terrain, especially across the Continental Divide. \nIncreasing southwest flow helps to develop lee troughing across the plains \nbringing breezy south to southwest winds and possibly a few storms along said \nboundary. Highs warm back into the 90s across the plains and remain in the 60s, \n70s and 80s across the higher terrain. \n\nFor Monday and Tuesday, moist southwesterly flow continues across the \nregion, with increasing uvv ahead of the passing upper system bringing\ngood chances of precipitation across the higher terrain Monday and \nTuesday, with the systems passing cold front Monday night bringing \nchances of precipitation to eastern Colorado into Tuesday. Temperatures\nat and slightly above seasonal levels on Monday, cool to below seasonal\non Tuesday, with highs in the 70s to low 80s across the plains, and \nmainly 50s and 60s across the higher terrain, save for 70s across\nthe high mountain valleys on Tuesday. \n\nMonsoonal moisture looks to remain in place within modest west to \nsouthwest flow aloft across the region through the end of next week, \nleading to continued daily chances of precipitation, as well as \ntemperatures remaining around seasonal levels.",
